%S A399875 1,1,2,16,284,10310,734912,103000974,28619480890,15851350023284,
%T A399875 17540109244191568,38805237723060061712,171690302550258993274912,
%U A399875 1519254275147952012900917492,26887606868565981206780269783812,951723762325850028465314391220874816
%N A399875 Number of unlabeled reducible flow graphs with n nodes containing a global source and a global sink, self-loops disallowed.
%C A399875 The first five terms coincide with A102599, which counts unrelated objects (connected oriented mating graphs), but the sequences differ from n = 6 on: a(6) = 10310 while A102599(6) = 12717.
%C A399875 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968).
%D A399875 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A399875 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399875 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399875 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399875 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A399875 a(n) = (1/(n-2)!) * Sum over cycle types mu of n-2 elements of permcount(mu) * F_S2(mu) for n >= 2, with a(1)=1, where F_S2 is the equivariant single-source region recurrence with the co-reachability inclusion-exclusion for the fixed sink.
%o A399875 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_ss_single_sink", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A399875 Cf. A397968 (entry-pointed family), A350794 (all such digraphs), A102599.
%K A399875 nonn,new
%O A399875 1,3
%A A399875 _Gregory Morse_, Sep 14 2026
